  "description": "LUXTAB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H80 N4 O20 Sm4,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.765-4.000 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.76-112.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H88N4O22Sm4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
